# G107 — Budget Tracker

*v2. See `budget-tracker.md` for prose: envelope model, category status over
time-window, budget alerts at 80%/100%/over, uncategorized spending surfaces
as suggestions for new envelopes.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Vault Monthly Budget

[monthly-budget @budget-path @year @month
    IN ORDER TO
        show the user their envelope status for the current month
        alert on overages or near-overages
        and suggest envelopes for uncategorized spending

    @budget <- [budget[from-yaml {path: @budget-path}]]
    @month-start <- [clock[start-of-month {year: @year, month: @month}]]
    @month-end   <- [clock[start-of-month {year: @year, month: @month + 1}]]

    @status <- [budget[status-between {budget: @budget,
                                         from-ms: @month-start,
                                         to-ms: @month-end}]]
    #envelopes @status

    @alerts <- @status where alert is true
    @alerts
        where count at least 1
        [notify[send {channels: ["email"],
                       message: "Budget alerts: " + @alerts:categories:joined}]]

    @uncategorised <- @status
        where budgeted-cents is zero and spent-cents > 0
    @uncategorised
        where count at least 1
        [ui[suggest-envelopes {candidates: @uncategorised}]]
]

---

## Verb Surface

[budget
    new
    add-envelope                  {budget, envelope}
    from-yaml                     {path}
    record                        {budget, transaction}
    status-between                {budget, from-ms, to-ms}
    status-all                    {budget}
    alerts                        {budget}
    total-budgeted                {budget}
    total-spent-between           {budget, from-ms, to-ms}
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: alert threshold as `where` derived

[@status
    where spent-cents at least 0.8 × budgeted-cents
    marks the envelope with alert: "near-limit"

@status
    where spent-cents at least budgeted-cents
    marks the envelope with alert: "over"

@status
    where budgeted-cents is zero and spent-cents > 0
    marks the envelope with alert: "uncategorized"
]

The resolver emits `alert` as a derived field; the choreography filters
on it without computing thresholds itself.

---

## Demo

[demo
    @b <- [budget[new]]
    [budget[add-envelope {budget: @b, envelope: {category: "groceries",
                                                    budgeted-cents: 40000}}]]
    [budget[record {budget: @b,
                     transaction: {category: "groceries",
                                    amount-cents: 15000,
                                    ts-ms: @last-week}}]]
    [budget[record {budget: @b,
                     transaction: {category: "coffee",
                                    amount-cents: 2500,
                                    ts-ms: @yesterday}}]]

    @status <- [budget[status-all {budget: @b}]]
    -> @status where category is "groceries"   ;; -> spent 15000 / budgeted 40000
    -> @status where category is "coffee"       ;; -> uncategorized alert
]
